# Sitemap structure that works

Do not use Next.js `app/sitemap.ts` or `app/robots.ts`. GSC often cannot fetch those (500, 406, `vary: rsc` headers, or HTML). Match Enclave: static files in `public/`.

## Files

- `public/sitemap.xml` — real XML, not a metadata route
- `public/robots.txt` — points at the sitemap on the **Search Console property host**

```
User-agent: *
Allow: /

Sitemap: https://arbourviewhomes.ca/sitemap.xml
```

## XML shape

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://arbourviewhomes.ca/</loc>
    <lastmod>2026-09-06T00:00:00.000Z</lastmod>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
```

- Keep the XML declaration
- Homepage `<loc>` has a trailing slash; other paths do not (`trailingSlash: false`)
- `priority` is `1.0`, not `1`
- Every `<loc>` must be the same host as the GSC property (this site: **apex** `arbourviewhomes.ca`, not `www`)

## Headers (`next.config.ts`)

- Sitemap: `Content-Type: text/xml; charset=UTF-8`, `Content-Disposition: inline; filename="sitemap.xml"`, `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
- Middleware must exclude `robots.txt` and `sitemap` from host redirects

## Why GSC says "Sitemap could not be read"

1. Sitemap URL **redirects** (308 apex → www). Google will not follow that for sitemaps.
2. Sitemap host **does not match** the GSC property (www file on an `arbourviewhomes.ca` property).
3. Dynamic `app/sitemap.ts` instead of `public/sitemap.xml`.

`SITE_URL`, middleware canonical host, Vercel Domains redirect, sitemap `<loc>`s, and GSC must all be **apex**. In Vercel: `arbourviewhomes.ca` is primary; `www` redirects to apex.

Submit only `https://arbourviewhomes.ca/sitemap.xml` on the apex property, then resubmit after a deploy.
